# Overtime & Working Time Policy (2024)

## 1. Scope

All employees except members of the Management Committee (see work regulations, annex 2).

## 2. Limits

Maximum 9 hours per day and 45 hours per week without prior legal justification; absolute ceilings of 11 hours per day and 50 hours per week. Minimum 11 hours of rest between two working days.

## 3. Prior approval

3.1 Overtime must be **requested in writing by the manager in advance** (e-mail or the "OT request" form in the timesheet tool).

3.2 **Overtime not approved in advance will not be compensated.**

3.3 Managers must ensure that planning allows work to be done within normal hours.

## 4. Compensation

Approved overtime gives right to: overtime premium of 50% (100% on Sundays and public holidays), and compensatory rest, unless the employee opts for voluntary overtime under the applicable legal regime.

## 5. Recording

Hours are recorded daily in the timesheet tool and via badge. Managers validate timesheets weekly. **Managers may correct timesheets that contain errors; corrections must be explained to the employee.**

## 6. Contact

Questions: hr@tectonic-solutions.be

