# On-call & Stand-by Policy – Support team (2025)

## 1. Rota

Support engineers take part in an on-call rota of **one week in five** (Monday 18:00 to Monday 08:00). The rota is published quarterly.

## 2. Availability

While on call, the engineer must be reachable by phone and able to **start working remotely within 30 minutes** of a P1/P2 page. No presence at the office is required. The engineer is free to stay at home or elsewhere within reach of an internet connection.

## 3. Stand-by allowance

A flat **stand-by allowance of €150 gross per on-call week** is paid.

## 4. Interventions

4.1 **Interventions shorter than 60 minutes are covered by the stand-by allowance.**

4.2 For interventions longer than 60 minutes, the time beyond the first 60 minutes is recorded in the timesheet as working time and compensated according to the Overtime & Working Time Policy.

4.3 Interventions are logged in the ticketing system; VPN connection logs are kept by IT Security for 12 months for security purposes.

## 5. Rest

After a night intervention of more than 2 hours, the engineer may start the next working day 3 hours later.

Nicolas Hubert, Support Manager – approved by Catherine Lemaire, HR Director, 20/01/2025

