author_role: HR Director
date: 2025-01-06
effective_from: 2025-01-01
jurisdiction: BE
language: en
themes: [T5, T4]
status: active
signed: true
formality: policy_approved_by_management
related_questions: [Q09, Q10]
---
# Performance Management & Bonus Policy (2025)

## 1. Cycle

- January: annual review and objective setting.
- July: mid-year review (formal rating).
- Ratings: **Exceeds (5) / Meets+ (4) / Meets (3) / Partially meets (2) / Below (1)**.

## 2. Objectives

2.1 Objectives are SMART and linked to the role.
2.2 **Objectives are pro-rated for part-time employees and for employees on statutory leave** (parental leave, time credit, maternity, long sickness) in proportion to the time actually worked.
2.3 **Availability on days not worked because of statutory leave may not be used as an evaluation criterion.**

## 3. Calibration

Ratings are calibrated by HR and the department head. A rating of 2 or lower must be supported by documented examples.

## 4. Bonus

Annual bonus (CCT 90 plan) target = 8% of annual gross salary, multiplied by the rating factor: 5 → 1.3; 4 → 1.1; 3 → 1.0; 2 → 0.5; 1 → 0. The mid-year rating counts for 40% of the bonus factor.

## 5. Appeals

An employee may contest a rating with the HR Director within 15 days.

