---
# IT Acceptable Use & Monitoring Policy (2024)

Owner: IT Security – approved by the Management Committee on 8 April 2024.

## 1. Company property

All IT systems, devices, e-mail accounts and data are company property and are provided for business use.

## 2. Acceptable use

- Limited private use is tolerated if it does not interfere with work.
- No storage of company data on private devices or personal cloud accounts.
- Use of personal e-mail for company documents is forbidden.

## 3. Monitoring

3.1 IT Security monitors network traffic, DLP events, VPN connections and security logs.

3.2 **Tectonic may access, inspect and read any mailbox, file or device at any time and without notice for any legitimate business reason**, including investigations into misconduct or leaks.

3.3 Employees have no expectation of privacy on company systems.

## 4. Logs

Security logs (VPN, DLP, proxy) are retained for 12 months. They are **confidential security data** and are not shared outside IT Security, except with the Management Committee or HR in investigations.

## 5. Sanctions

Breaches may lead to disciplinary sanctions up to dismissal for serious cause.

Kristof Janssens, IT Security Manager

@@@ FILE POL-DLP-2025
---
folder: 05_company_policies
format: md
title: Data Loss Prevention (DLP) Standard
doc_type: standard
author: Kristof Janssens
author_role: IT Security Manager
date: 2025-06-02
jurisdiction: BE
language: en
themes: [T6, T1]
status: active
signed: false
formality: technical_standard
related_questions: [Q01]
---
# DLP Standard (June 2025)

## Scope
Microsoft 365 DLP policies on e-mail, OneDrive, SharePoint and endpoint (browser uploads).

## Detection rules
- R1: upload of files labelled *Confidential* to non-corporate cloud storage.
- R2: e-mail forwarding of *Confidential* files to external private domains (gmail.com, hotmail.com, outlook.com, ...).
- R3: export of > 1,000 CRM records within 24 h.

## Escalation
1. Alert reviewed by IT Security within 1 working day.
2. Confirmed high-severity alerts are **reported to the HR Director and the employee's line manager within 24 hours**, with the evidence (file names, timestamps, destination).
3. HR decides on further steps. IT Security does not contact the employee.

## Evidence
Only DLP metadata (who, what, when, where) is used for the alert. Access to mailbox **content** requires a separate written request of the HR Director and must follow the CCT 81 individualisation procedure.

